  "final_message": "I have started checking the repository status and will inspect the codebase as soon as the command completes.\nI have run `npm test` and am waiting for the test suite to finish.\nWaiting for the build and test suite to complete.\nI cannot remove `channel` from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event and the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/GEMINI.md#L27-L28):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this cannot be removed directly:\n1. **External Contract Break**: Even if `channel` is not read internally within `orders-service`, [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published to downstream services in other repositories (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing the field is a breaking, non-additive schema change that could disrupt deployed consumers.\n2. **Model Dependency**: Removing `channel` from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) / [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/order.ts#L32-L38) breaks [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59), as well as the input contract for `POST /orders`.\n\n### Recommended deprecation procedure:\n1. Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/order.ts#L32-L38) / [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29).\n2. Coordinate with the downstream teams (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) to ensure their consumer models are updated and deployed.\n3. Once all deployed consumers no longer depend on `channel`, execute the removal alongside the required schema version bump.\n",
